{
  "_comment": [
    "Each weapon's play settings (docs/gameplay/07_GAMEPLAY_PLAN.md §5.6; src/core/game/systems/weapon_play.h).",
    "missBack: how far a miss sends the combo back, by weapon level. The entry with the highest lv at or below the",
    "weapon's level applies; back is a number of points, or \"start\". The owner's example (2026-10-20): Lv 5 back to the",
    "start, Lv 10 back 5 points, Lv 15 back 4 ... A level below every entry also goes back to the start.",
    "missWaitMs: after a miss, how long before the next tap counts (the sword puts itself back).",
    "Keys: an items.json weapon id, \"unarmed\" (no weapon worn), or \"default\" (any weapon without its own entry).",
    "Battle v3's point play (docs/gameplay/07 §4, §5.1; phase 1, the owner 2026-10-22): levels: per weapon level, the points on the",
    "combo track (1-5) and the attribute bonuses it gives (data/stats.json ids). usesToLevel: wins needed from Lv 1 to 2,",
    "2 to 3, ... (the level stops at the last levels entry). turnBack: the marker turns back at the ends; false: one sweep.",
    "sweepMs: one sweep with no charge; maxSweeps: turning back, the combo ends after this many. chargeMs: waiting this long",
    "fills the charge; chargeSpeedUp / chargeDamage: a full charge makes the marker and the damage this much more (1 = x2).",
    "hitWindow: how close a tap must be to a point (a fraction of the track). The values are first guesses (made up for now).",
    "fx: the battle's particles by weapon level (media/fx/battle.particle): the entry with the highest lv at or",
    "below the level plays; release at the player as the attack goes off, hit at the monster with the damage number.",
    "A weapon without fx uses the default entry's.",
    "hitWindowMs: the window is never shorter than this in time, so a faster (charged) marker keeps it; lateMs: a tap",
    "this long after the marker passed a point still counts (touch delay). Both default to 140 / 80 (the owner 2026-10-24:",
    "the timing was too hard); a window is never more than 45% of the gap between two points.",
    "results (docs/gameplay/13 §4.2, the owner 2026-10-25): what an attack does by how many points it matched; the highest",
    "row reached applies (hits: a number, or \"all\" = every point of the level). damage: times the hit; fx: replaces the",
    "level's hit effect; anim: the player's clip; sound; stunMs: the monster stops; pushMs: its attack clock goes back;",
    "breakAdd: more on its break gauge. A weapon without results uses the default entry's.",
    "pace: \"cooldown\" or \"stamina\" for this weapon (empty: data/battle.json's; 13 §6.3).",
    "move: a result row's named move (a text.json key, docs/gameplay/07 §5.4 and 15 §3.3), shown over the monster.",
    "play: the weapon's own attack (docs/gameplay/15 §3.3, touch_play.h): track (the point track), bow (drag back and let go at the target), slice (swipe the arrows' ways), circles (tap each circle as its ring closes). Each counts its points like the track, so the results, fx and clips stay the same. Scenarios play the track unless their battle sets \"play\"."
  ],
